-- title:
--   An O-point of D whose Poincaré class is M
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $\mathfrak X$ a `DRModelPackage` for $p$ (so in particular a proper flat integral model `DRModel p` over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$ with its sections $\varepsilon_\infty,\varepsilon_0$), $O$ a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, $\kappa$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ together with a ring homomorphism $O\to\kappa$, and $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}$ a `DRResolvedModelPackage` for these data, with structure morphism $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toBase}\colon Y\to\operatorname{Spec}O$ and morphism $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toDR}\colon Y\to \mathfrak X_O$, where $\mathfrak X_O$ denotes the fibre product of `DRModel.toBase p` with $\operatorname{Spec}O\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$. Let $D$ be a `RelativePic0Designation` over $\mathbb Z$ for `DRModel.toBase p`, i.e. a scheme $D.P$ with a structure morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$ and a zero section, and let $h_D$ witness that $D$ represents the subfunctor of rigidified line bundles along $\varepsilon_\infty$ cut out by the condition `algEquivZeroCut`, namely that on every geometric fibre the bundle be algebraically equivalent to zero in the sense of `IsAlgEquivZero`; $h_D$ supplies the Poincaré bundle $h_D.\mathrm{poincare}$ on $\mathfrak X_{D.P}$ and the universal property. Let $m\in\mathbb N$, let $\sigma_0,\dots,\sigma_{m-1}$ be sections of $Y\to\operatorname{Spec}O$, let $\mathrm{pos},\mathrm{neg}\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\mathbb N$, assume each $\sigma_j$ carries the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}O$ into the locus $\mathfrak X_{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{smoothOffEdges}$, and assume $\sum_j(\mathrm{pos}_j-\mathrm{neg}_j)=0$ in $\mathbb Z$. Let $M$ be an invertible sheaf of modules on $\mathfrak X_O$ such that, after pulling back along $Y_{\mathrm{Frac}(O)}\to Y\to\mathfrak X_O$, it is isomorphic to the iterated tensor product, over $j$ in order, of the dual of the $\mathrm{pos}_j$-th power of the ideal sheaf of the section $\sigma_j$ with the module of the $\mathrm{neg}_j$-th power of that ideal sheaf, the fold starting from the tensor unit on $Y_{\mathrm{Frac}(O)}$; and such that for every algebraically closed field $k$ and every morphism $s\colon\operatorname{Spec}k\to\operatorname{Spec}O$ whose image contains the closed point of $O$, the restriction of $M$ to the fibre of $\mathfrak X_O$ over $s$ satisfies `IsAlgEquivZero`, i.e. it is connected to the trivial bundle by an invertible sheaf on a family over a geometrically integral base locally of finite type over $k$ specialising at two $k$-points to the trivial bundle and to the restriction of $M$. Then there is a morphism $z\colon\operatorname{Spec}O\to D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$, that is with $z$ followed by $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb Z\to O$, such that the line bundle underlying the pullback of $h_D.\mathrm{poincare}$ along $z$ is isomorphic to $M$.
--
--   This is the integral Abel–Jacobi step on the Deligne–Rapoport model: a divisor class on the model over a discrete valuation ring which is a degree-zero combination of smooth sections on the generic fibre and is algebraically equivalent to zero on the geometric fibres over the closed point is classified by an $O$-point of the representing scheme $D$ of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$-cut. It is used in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_schemeHomOver_of_comp_eq_zero_of_abelJacobiPin_of_surjective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_schemeHomOver_of_comp_eq_zero_of_abelJacobiPin_of_surjective), where such $O$-points furnish the integral points needed for the specialisation of divisor classes on modular curves.
